WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:06.380
- [Mark] Toya, where
are you from originally?

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.213
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:09.390
- [Toya] Um, Los Angeles, California.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.227
- [Mark] And you grew
up with both parents?

00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:13.910
- [Toya] I grew up with,
on 108th and Central,

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.600
with not my dad, just my
mother and my grandmother.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.950
- [Mark] Okay.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.133
And how was your childhood, generally?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.133
- I had an abusive childhood.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.960
I was abused by my brother a lot.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.970
He beat me up til he beat
me unconscious one time.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.730
I was in the hospital
for two days for that.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.550
Um, he was very, like, irate
without through his life,

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.930
he had a lot of, growing up,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.750
bad things that happened to him,

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.050
so it reflected on us,

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.700
and he took his anger and abuse out on us.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.040
- [Mark] What about, did your mom step in

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:46.990
and protect you, or?

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.100
- My mom really didn't
step in and protect me.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.540
I was raised in a Christian home,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.520
so it was more so that
whatever happened to you,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.720
just let God forgive them for it

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.550
and God will take care of the problem.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.690
It was more so that, it
never really wasn't no,

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.990
you know, let's get the police involved

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.160
or anything like that,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.709
but my brother beat me for years.

00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:10.379
- [Mark] Wow. That's terrible.

00:01:10.379 --> 00:01:11.212
- Yeah.

00:01:11.212 --> 00:01:14.720
- [Mark] And then, eventually
you guys got older.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.400
- When we got older, the last time,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.180
I'm 39, so the last time he
put his hands on me I was 24.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.280
- [Mark] Oh, so it continued?

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.150
- Yeah, it continued for a while.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.750
Um, I had a baby brother
that was abusive also,

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.390
and one time I was driving,

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.710
I was at church, this happened at church,

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.423
and um, they got upset because

00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:35.930
they wanted to use my car
to go to Marina Valley,

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.930
and I wouldn't allow them to use my car,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.760
so my baby brother jumped on me

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.740
and, um, he tried to beat me up,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.290
and it happened at church,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.210
and I ended up taking my
car and I tried to run away,

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.950
but the car ended up
spinning out of control

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.400
and it almost hit my
brother, and he almost died.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.970
- [Mark] Where do you think
their anger came from?

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.660
- I think a lot of their
anger and frustration

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.870
came from my father.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.030
My father was abusive towards my mother,

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.920
he beat her for 11 years,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.180
til one time that she was
blind for like four days.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.640
So, I think it came from
my father, so to speak.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.639
- [Mark] Yeah, that would make sense.

00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:13.250
- Yeah.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.759
- [Mark] Wow.

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:15.860
So your dad was in your lives for a while?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.963
- He was, he was in and
out of my life for a while.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.250
The last time I had talked
and spoken with my father

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.990
when he found out what happened,

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.430
it was after me getting
raped by my cousin.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.510
I got raped by my first cousin, um,

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.140
by the name of Dejan Taylor.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.570
He raped me when I was 15 years old.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.040
He molested me for like four years,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.620
then he raped me after that,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.380
so he was molesting me when I was a child.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.610
- [Mark] Oh, so even
before that, he was...

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.720
- Yeah, he was molesting
me when I was a child,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.981
and my parents, my mother
believed the story,

00:02:47.981 --> 00:02:50.220
but my auntie didn't believe the story,

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.750
which was his mother.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.390
Um, she passed away by him.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.793
He drowned his mother.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.487
- [Mark] Did he get caught?

00:02:58.487 --> 00:02:59.710
- No, he didn't get caught.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.530
They just didn't see it as a drowning.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.920
They seen it he was trying to help her.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.770
So, he's been running for some years,

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.665
but they didn't see it as that.

00:03:07.665 --> 00:03:09.454
- [Mark] Oh.

00:03:09.454 --> 00:03:12.430
So do you talk with your family still?

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.180
- [Toya] I don't really
speak with my family.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.830
Um, every now and then,

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.510
I have a sister I go to church with,

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.510
I speak with her from time to time,

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.270
but I don't really talk
to my family like that.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.600
We don't really have a
connection like that.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.750
- [Mark] And so eventually
you left home on your own?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.350
- [Toya] I went out on
my own at the age of 18

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.920
and then I went to CCC,
California Conservation Corps,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.960
and then I ran into this lady
by the name of Andrea Johnson,

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.820
she ended up becoming my godmother,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.270
and then I was on my own
with her for a while,

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.610
and then I ventured off

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.890
because I ended up being a lesbian

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.100
and I was in a relationship
with this girl,

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.650
so my family was always against
my homosexual lifestyle,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.710
and that's where a lot
of abuse came from, too,

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.070
because they didn't want me to be gay,

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.850
they felt that putting their hands on me,

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.430
or, you know, speaking
to me some type of way,

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.410
that it was gonna change the
fact of who I was and who I am,

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.020
which that doesn't have
that, that's not gonna work,

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.520
so they judged me a lot,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.750
so I was on my own for a while,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.260
and then I end up moving in
with my first girlfriend,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.490
and we was together for like five years.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.930
It was a cool relationship,

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.310
but it was a lot of abuse, too,

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.340
and neglect in that relationship,

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.240
because I found myself doing,
repeating that same cycle,

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.910
putting my hands on her,

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.240
I was fighting her a lot,

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.800
so, but it came from a lot of hurt

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.270
and pain and abuse from my childhood,

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:35.270
and then at the age of 26,
27, I end up going to jail,

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.740
then I end up going to prison,

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.470
and I did my time in prison,

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.570
I was in prison for a couple of years,

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.290
and then I got out on parole,

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:47.120
and after I paroled I
came down here to Skid Row

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.400
and I stayed at the Weingart,

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.670
and then I was at the Weingart
for like a couple of months

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.430
before I became on Skid Row,

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.160
and then I was, like, in and out,

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.620
so I just got outta
prison not too long ago.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.260
I did another prison term,

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.120
I just got out of prison not too long ago,

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.790
on May 4th I was released, of this year,

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:05.980
so I've been, like,

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.358
living here and there and here and there.

00:05:08.358 --> 00:05:10.683
- [Mark] What were you in
prison for, the two times?

00:05:10.683 --> 00:05:13.470
- I was, my first term
was a terrorist threat.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.790
It was assault on a police officer.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.300
I ended up putting my hands on a cop,

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.763
I fought the police and then
my second term was grand theft.

00:05:24.037 --> 00:05:26.200
- [Mark] And, so you're
living on the street now?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.190
- Yes.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.693
- [Mark] And are you
using any of the drugs

00:05:28.693 --> 00:05:29.653
that are out here?

00:05:29.653 --> 00:05:30.652
- I use crystal.

00:05:30.652 --> 00:05:32.814
- [Mark] Crystal, how long
have you been using that for?

00:05:32.814 --> 00:05:36.892
- I've been on crystal for like two years.

00:05:36.892 --> 00:05:38.580
- [Mark] And were you using
any drugs before that?

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.473
- No I wasn't.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:41.810
And then it was pills,

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:45.200
I was using, taking pharmaceutical
drugs, which is pills.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.763
I was on pills for, like, nine years.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:52.430
Taking narcos and somas
to take away my pain

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.560
or just numb me to the
fact of what's going on

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.090
in my life, you know?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.530
Not having a father being there for me,

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:01.610
and me and my mother not
having a real close connection,

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.030
you know, I was doing that for a while.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:08.010
I overdosed one time in my house.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.000
My neighbor came and
she found me and I was,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.070
or I had overdosed from the
pills that I was taking,

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:18.070
so that kinda lured me to try
and stop me from taking them,

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.730
but I haven't really stopped taking them,

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.603
I take them every now and then.

00:06:23.957 --> 00:06:25.750
- [Mark] And what do you do for money now?

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.110
- Well, I'm not working
at this current moment.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.460
I'm with a temp agency,

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.900
so I'm trying to get work through them,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:34.450
but I'm not really employed right now, so.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.490
- [Mark] I mean, there's a lot of ways

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.171
for unemployed people to make
money out here on the street.

00:06:37.171 --> 00:06:39.163
- It's a lot of selling drugs.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.890
What I used to do when I wasn't working,

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.573
I've robbed people before.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.220
That was my making my wheels

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.800
and making my meals and making money.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.680
There was one time I even robbed

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.520
this neighborhood weed store.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:55.783
I robbed them.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.780
I've did a lot, I did, uh,

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:05.320
fake checks, fake
identity, false identity,

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.700
identity theft, I did that too.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:09.533
- [Mark] Just trying to survive.

00:07:09.533 --> 00:07:10.990
- [Toya] Trying to make it.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:11.940
It's hard out here.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.920
- [Mark] Yeah, I've heard it all.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.260
All right, Toya, thank you
so much for talking to me.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.093
- [Toya] You're welcome.

00:07:18.093 --> 00:07:19.480
- [Mark] And sharing your story.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:20.338
- Thank you.

00:07:20.338 --> 00:07:21.171
- [Mark] Good luck with everything.

00:07:21.171 --> 00:07:22.004
- Okay.

00:07:22.004 --> 00:07:22.837
- [Mark] Thank you.

00:07:22.837 --> 00:07:23.670
- All right, you're welcome.

